From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sourab Gupta <sougupta@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:07:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: Patch NFS driver to support GDS

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167898

With this change, the NFS driver would be enabled to support
GPUDirectStorage(GDS). The change is around frwr_map and frwr_unmap in
the NFS driver, where the IO request is first intercepted to check for GDS
pages and if it is a GDS page then the request is served by GDS driver
component called nvidia-fs, else the request would be served by the
standard NFS driver code.

Signed-off-by: Sourab Gupta <sougupta@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit e4a7d2426aa277b9c7fdf004a3773c358624f5b8 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00698
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@4535ba20ee05c51d5314a897958480d5c2d7626e
---
